---
type: agent/instruction
description: Report the current client Git worktree inventory
usage: "guide://_worktree/list"
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
---
Run `git worktree list --porcelain` in the current worktree. Convert its `worktree`
records into a JSON array of absolute path strings, then send the result through
`{{tool_prefix}}send_file_content` with the exact opaque path
`.git-worktrees.json`. Do not create that file in the project.

For example:

```json
["{{project.root}}", "{{project.root}}_languid-lizard"]
```

The report is client discovery data. After sending it, request the worktree
command you intend to use. Guide caches this inventory for 90 seconds; refresh
it after creating or removing a worktree, or when Guide asks for a fresh report.

{{#kwargs.verbose}}
For every listed worktree, read its configured workflow file and report the
observed `worktree`, `phase`, and `issue` values. Treat an unavailable workflow
file as unavailable state; do not use handoff context as a workflow-state source.
{{/kwargs.verbose}}
